Third-party data
----------------

The repository ships some data that comes, in whole or in part, from third
parties. Each file below names its source in its own header, or in the file
named beside it. assets/SOURCES.tsv records the source, version, licence and
header of every data file the repository ships; `og dev licences check`, run
by the Lint workflow, fails when a file under assets/ has no row there, when
a file lacks the header its row names, or when this file does not name a
third-party row. The licence texts these sources ask us to keep are in
assets/licences/.

assets/acmg_sf.tsv
    ACMG SF v3.3 secondary-findings genes: Lee et al., Genet Med
    2025;27(8):101454, doi:10.1016/j.gim.2025.101454, Table 1. The gene list
    is facts; the table_text column holds short cited quotations of a
    factual reporting rule.

assets/bloodtype_markers.tsv
    Blood-group variants as packaged by RBCeq2 2.4.4 (database v2.5.1),
    Copyright 2025 Australian Red Cross Lifeblood, MIT licence
    (assets/licences/RBCeq2-LICENSE.txt). Names follow the ISBT nomenclature.

assets/callability_genes.tsv
    NIST Genome in a Bottle CMRG v1.00 and GRCh38 stratifications v3.6, not
    subject to US copyright (assets/licences/NIST-GIAB-NOTICE.txt);
    GENCODE 50, open access.

assets/carrier_genes.tsv
    Gene spans from GENCODE release 50, open access. Gene lists from Gregg et
    al., Genet Med 2021, ACOG Committee Opinions 690 and 691, and Orphadata
    (en_product6 and en_product9_ages of 2026-06-23), CC BY 4.0,
    https://www.orphadata.com.

assets/chip_genes_grch38.bed
    Gene records of GENCODE release 50, open access, no restriction on use.

assets/licences/
    The licence texts of the sources in this list, each under its own terms.

assets/locityper_loci.bed
    Timofey Prodanov, Locityper loci database,
    https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.15879519, CC BY 4.0. Changed: six loci
    kept, two joined.

assets/ownhealth/genome-facts.v1.json
assets/ownhealth/sensitive_genes.tsv
    Copied byte for byte from OwnHealth, https://github.com/GeiserX/OwnHealth,
    under its licence, AGPL-3.0 (assets/ownhealth/VENDORED.tsv names the
    commit and the sha256 of each file).

assets/par_grch38.bed
    The GRCh38 pseudoautosomal regions of the Genome Reference Consortium,
    https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/grc/human (docs/03-variant-calling.md). The
    file has no header because its readers take every line as an interval.

assets/parascopy_models_v1.7.txt
    Timofey Prodanov, Parascopy precomputed data,
    https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.15019940, CC BY 4.0. Changed: only the
    model regions are kept, one per line, overlapping copies merged.

assets/reference/cytoBand.hg38.txt
    UCSC Genome Browser chromosome bands for hg38, freely usable for any
    purpose. Credit: the UCSC Genome Browser Group, University of
    California, Santa Cruz (assets/reference/README.md).

assets/sv_rule_regions.tsv
    TRExplorer catalog, Copyright (c) 2024 Broad Institute, MIT licence
    (assets/licences/TRExplorer-LICENSE.txt); GENCODE, open access; HGNC and
    NCBI assembly regions, no restriction on use.

assets/ystr_panel.tsv
    The marker order, names and panels of FamilyTreeDNA's Y-111 test,
    reproduced only so that counts line up with FamilyTreeDNA results; no
    FamilyTreeDNA text is copied. FamilyTreeDNA is a trademark of Gene by
    Gene, Ltd., which does not endorse this table. Regions from
    HipSTR-references (MIT); motifs from NIST STRBase.

tests/fixtures/consumer_export/sites.tsv.gz
    23andMe v5 site list from 23andme2vcf, Copyright (c) 2015 Rob Long, MIT
    licence (assets/licences/23andme2vcf-LICENSE.txt); NCBI dbSNP b157, no
    restriction on use (tests/fixtures/consumer_export/README.md).

The og binaries
---------------

The og binaries also link third-party code. Each release ships their notices
in THIRD-PARTY-LICENSES.txt, written by `og dev licences notices`.
